---
interface Props { kind: 'rollout' | 'race' | 'cursor'; }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const definitions = {
  rollout: { n: 1, title: 'Keep an accepted route through the change', option: '', choices: [], stages: [
    'Only price exists. Old callers read and write it.',
    'Expand: add a nullable price_hundredths. Old callers still use price; new values may be missing.',
    'Deploy bridge callers: read price, write both values in one transaction. Drain every old-only writer before continuing.',
    'Backfill and reconcile while bridge writes preserve agreement. Readers still use price.',
    'Switch reads to price_hundredths. Keep writing both forms while a return to bridge readers is promised.',
    'Contract after old dependencies and return targets retire. Prepare old-column requirements, then stop maintaining and remove price.'
  ]},
  race: { n: 2, title: 'A repeated write can still be stale', option: 'Backfill write', choices: [['stale','Assign the earlier 2000'],['guard','Require the earlier price'],['current','Convert the current price']], stages: [
    'P7 starts at 20.00, with no new value. A backfill worker is about to read it.',
    'The worker reads 20.00 and calculates 2000. This local copy does not protect the database row.',
    'A bridge caller commits 22.00 and 2200 together. The worker still remembers 2000.',
    'The worker now attempts its write. Compare each rule against the row that the bridge caller committed.'
  ]},
  cursor: { n: 3, title: 'A last key does not account for every row', option: 'Late insert', choices: [['bridge','Bridge writes 8.00 and 800'],['old','Old-only writer leaves NULL']], stages: [
    'The backfill visits P3 and commits its new value 450. Its durable cursor is P3.',
    'P11 arrives after that commit. In the stated text order P11 sorts before P3, behind the cursor.',
    'The remaining scan visits P7 and P9, then ends at P9. It never visits P11.',
    'Reconcile the whole required population. The insert rule determines whether the late row is ready.'
  ]}
};
const d = definitions[kind];
---
<figure class="migration-figure" data-migration={kind} aria-labelledby={`migration-${kind}-title`}>
  <figcaption id={`migration-${kind}-title`}><span>Figure {d.n}</span> {d.title}</figcaption>
  <div class="mf-panel">
    {d.option && <label class="mf-option">{d.option}<select aria-label={d.option}>{d.choices.map(([value,label]) => <option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>}
    <p class="mf-model">Illustrative {kind === 'rollout' ? 'deployment states' : kind === 'race' ? 'ordering of committed changes' : 'text-key scan, P11 < P3 < P7 < P9'}</p>
    {kind === 'rollout' && <>
      <ol class="mf-route" aria-label="Migration phases">{['Old','Expand','Bridge','Backfill','New reads','Contract'].map((label,i)=><li data-phase={i}>{label}</li>)}</ol>
      <div class="mf-dual">
        <div class="mf-box"><span>products · P7</span><dl><dt>price</dt><dd data-old data-live>20.00</dd><dt>price_hundredths</dt><dd data-new data-live>absent</dd></dl></div>
        <div class="mf-box"><span>Accepted callers</span><dl><dt>Read from</dt><dd data-read data-live>price</dd><dt>Write to</dt><dd data-write data-live>price</dd></dl></div>
      </div>
      <p class="mf-verdict" data-verdict data-live>Keep the old column for the callers using it.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'race' && <>
      <div class="mf-dual">
        <div class="mf-box"><span>Backfill worker · local memory</span><p class="mf-value" data-memory data-live>Nothing read</p><p data-action data-live>Waiting to read P7</p></div>
        <div class="mf-box"><span>Database · committed P7</span><dl><dt>price</dt><dd data-old data-live>20.00</dd><dt>price_hundredths</dt><dd data-new data-live>NULL</dd></dl></div>
      </div>
      <p class="mf-flow" data-flow data-live>Worker → read → database</p>
      <p class="mf-verdict" data-verdict data-live>Missing: 1 · disagrees with price: 1</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'cursor' && <>
      <p class="mf-cursor" data-cursor data-live>Committed cursor: P3</p>
      <div class="mf-table"><table><caption>products in text-key order · committed values</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">price</th><th scope="col">Hundredths</th><th scope="col">Scan</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr data-row="P11" hidden><th scope="row">P11</th><td>8.00</td><td data-late data-live>800</td><td>Behind cursor</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">P3</th><td>4.50</td><td>450</td><td>Visited</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">P7</th><td>20.00</td><td data-p7 data-live>NULL</td><td data-s7 data-live>Not yet</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">P9</th><td>35.00</td><td data-p9 data-live>NULL</td><td data-s9 data-live>Not yet</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <p class="mf-verdict" data-verdict data-live>The cursor describes committed visits.</p>
    </>}
    <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{d.stages[0]}</p>
    <div class="mf-controls" role="group" aria-label={`Figure ${d.n} controls`}><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / {d.stages.length}</span><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="mf-caption">{kind === 'rollout' ? 'The data and caller rules change separately. A new column can exist long before its values are safe to read. The final state deliberately ends the return window.' : kind === 'race' ? 'Each option reuses the same ordering: worker read, bridge commit, worker write. No lock wait, elapsed time or concurrent-server execution is measured by this drawing.' : 'P11 is an independent migration arrival: Tea strainer, stock 0. The old-only option deliberately violates the chosen protocol; it shows why draining those writers is a precondition.'}</p>
  <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><ol>{d.stages.map(text=><li>{text}</li>)}</ol>{kind === 'race' && <p>The unguarded assignment ends at 22.00/2000. The source-price guard affects zero rows and leaves 22.00/2200; re-read and retry. Deriving from the current protected row also leaves 22.00/2200.</p>}{kind === 'cursor' && <p>A bridge insert leaves all four rows complete and equal to price × 100. An old-only insert leaves P11 missing; reaching P9 does not repair or even visit it.</p>}</details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-migration]')) {
    const kind = root.dataset.migration;
    const select = root.querySelector('select');
    const set = (selector: string, text: string) => { const element = root.querySelector(selector); if (element) element.textContent = text; };
    const rollout = [
      ['20.00','absent','price','price','Keep the old column for the callers using it.','Only price exists. Old callers read and write it.'],
      ['20.00','NULL','price','price','New reads are not yet allowed.','Expand: add a nullable price_hundredths. Old callers continue using price.'],
      ['20.00','NULL','price','both, atomically','Drain old-only writers and in-flight work.','Bridge callers initialise both forms on insert and change both together. Existing rows can still be missing the new value.'],
      ['20.00','2000','price','both, atomically','Reconcile coverage and price × 100 equality.','Backfill old rows while bridge callers preserve agreement. Keep reads on price until acceptance.'],
      ['20.00','2000','price_hundredths','both, atomically','Return to bridge reads remains possible.','New readers use 2000 with its hundredths unit. Both fields remain current during the return window.'],
      ['removed','2000','price_hundredths','price_hundredths','Returning now requires a new migration.','Retire old reads and return targets, prepare column requirements, then stop legacy writes and remove price.']
    ];
    const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => kind === 'rollout' ? 6 : 4, draw: (step: number) => {
      const option = select?.value;
      if (kind === 'rollout') {
        const state = rollout[step];
        ['[data-old]','[data-new]','[data-read]','[data-write]','[data-verdict]','[data-explanation]'].forEach((selector,i)=>set(selector,state[i]));
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-phase]').forEach((el,i)=> { el.classList.toggle('mf-active',i===step); if(i===step) el.setAttribute('aria-current','step'); else el.removeAttribute('aria-current'); });
      } else if (kind === 'race') {
        set('[data-memory]',step === 0 ? 'Nothing read' : '20.00 → 2000');
        set('[data-old]',step < 2 ? '20.00' : '22.00');
        set('[data-new]',step < 2 ? 'NULL' : step === 3 && option === 'stale' ? '2000' : '2200');
        const actions = ['Waiting to read P7','Calculated, but not written','Still holding the earlier 2000',option === 'stale' ? 'SET price_hundredths = 2000' : option === 'guard' ? 'WHERE price = 20.00 → 0 rows' : 'Convert the protected current price'];
        set('[data-action]',actions[step]);
        set('[data-flow]',step < 2 ? 'Worker → read → database' : step === 2 ? 'Bridge → commit 22.00 and 2200 → database' : option === 'stale' ? 'Worker → stale overwrite → database' : option === 'guard' ? 'Worker → guard fails → re-read before retry' : 'Worker → derive from protected row → 2200');
        set('[data-verdict]',step < 2 ? 'Missing: 1 · disagrees with price: 1' : step === 3 && option === 'stale' ? 'Missing: 0 · disagrees with price: 1' : 'Missing: 0 · disagrees with price: 0');
        const notes = ['P7 starts at 20.00 with no new value.','The worker reads 20.00. Its remembered value is not a lock.','The bridge caller commits 22.00 and 2200. Its newer value must survive the backfill.',option === 'stale' ? 'The worker stores 2000 over 2200. Repeating this assignment remains repeatable and wrong.' : option === 'guard' ? 'The source no longer equals 20.00. Zero affected rows leaves 2200 intact; account for the row by re-reading, rather than treating zero as success.' : 'The current 22.00 implies 2200, which is already stored. The conditional update leaves it alone; it never copies the remembered 2000.'];
        set('[data-explanation]',notes[step]);
      } else {
        const late = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-row="P11"]'); if(late) late.hidden = step === 0;
        set('[data-late]',option === 'old' ? 'NULL' : '800');
        set('[data-p7]',step < 2 ? 'NULL' : '2000'); set('[data-p9]',step < 2 ? 'NULL' : '3500');
        set('[data-s7]',step < 2 ? 'Not yet' : 'Visited'); set('[data-s9]',step < 2 ? 'Not yet' : 'Visited');
        set('[data-cursor]',step < 2 ? 'Committed cursor: P3' : 'Committed cursor: P9 · scan finished');
        set('[data-verdict]',step < 3 ? 'The cursor describes committed visits.' : option === 'old' ? 'Whole-table check: P11 missing · do not switch reads' : 'Whole-table check: 0 missing · 0 disagreements');
        const notes = ['P3 is committed at 4.50/450. P7 and P9 still await the backfill.','P11 is inserted behind P3 in this text ordering. ' + (option === 'old' ? 'The prohibited old-only writer leaves its new field NULL.' : 'The bridge caller writes 8.00 and 800 together.'),'P7 and P9 are converted. The scan reaches its last key without ever visiting P11.',option === 'old' ? 'Reconciliation finds P11 even though the scan finished. Close the old write path and repair the row before acceptance.' : 'P11 needed no visit: the bridge initialised it correctly. The scan plus the preserved write rule can converge.'];
        set('[data-explanation]',notes[step]);
      }
    }});
    select?.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  }
</script>
<style>
  .migration-figure { margin:2.4rem 0; font: .88rem/1.55 var(--font-sans); }
  figcaption { margin-bottom:.7rem; font:1.15rem/1.4 var(--font-serif); }
  figcaption > span { font:.68rem var(--font-sans); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; margin-right:.7rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .mf-panel { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); padding:1.1rem; }
  .mf-option { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.7rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:1rem; }
  select,button { color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-radius:4px; font:inherit; padding:.5rem .7rem; }
  select { max-width:100%; }
  button { cursor:pointer; min-height:42px; }
  button[aria-disabled="true"] { color:var(--color-text-secondary); border-style:dashed; }
  select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset:3px; }
  .mf-model { color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:0 0 1rem; font-size:.78rem; }
  .mf-route { list-style:none; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:.4rem; padding:0; margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .mf-route li { padding:.4rem; text-align:center; border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-radius:3px; }
  .mf-route li.mf-active { border:2px solid var(--color-accent); padding:calc(.4rem - 1px); font-weight:700; background:var(--color-surface); }
  .mf-dual { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.8rem; }
  .mf-box { border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); padding:.9rem; min-width:0; background:var(--color-surface); }
  .mf-box > span { display:block; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.78rem; margin-bottom:.7rem; }
  .mf-box dl { display:grid; gap:.4rem; margin:0; }
  dt { font: .75rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); overflow-wrap:anywhere; } dd { margin:0 0 .4rem; font-size:1.14rem; }
  .mf-box p { margin:0 0 .5rem; overflow-wrap:anywhere; } .mf-value { font-size:1.4rem; }
  .mf-flow,.mf-cursor { padding:.7rem; border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  .mf-verdict { margin:1rem 0; font-weight:600; }
  [data-explanation] { border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent); padding:.55rem .8rem; margin:1rem 0; min-height:4.6em; }
  .mf-controls { display:flex; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.45rem; border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding-top:.8rem; }
  [data-step] { margin-left:auto; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  [data-hold] { flex-basis:100%; height:3px; background:var(--color-rule); } [data-hold] span { display:block; height:100%; width:0; background:var(--color-accent); }
  .mf-caption { color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:.7rem 0; font-size:.8rem; }
  details { margin-top:.6rem; } summary { cursor:pointer; color:var(--color-accent); text-decoration:underline; } details ol { padding-left:1.4rem; }
  .mf-table { width:100%; } .mf-table table { display:table; width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-size:.8rem; margin:0; } caption { text-align:left; color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.75rem; margin-bottom:.5rem; }
  th,td { padding:.55rem .4rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); text-align:left; } [data-row="P11"] { outline:2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset:-2px; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { .mf-panel { padding:.8rem; } .mf-dual { grid-template-columns:1fr; } .mf-route { font-size:.75rem; } .mf-box dl { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr); column-gap:1rem; align-items:baseline; } dd { font-size:.95rem; overflow-wrap:anywhere; } th,td { font-size:.78rem; padding:.5rem .2rem; } }
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) { [data-hold] span { transition:none !important; } }
</style>
